Task: Configure Shared Storage Volume Across Multiple Containers

Context & Overview:
You are provided with three separate Dockerfiles (Dockerfile1, Dockerfile2, Dockerfile3) and a test data directory (./testdir/file.txt). In microservices and batch processing workflows, multiple containers often need access to a shared persistent volume to pass data between execution stages.

Your objective is to create a single shared Docker named volume called "shared-volume" and configure all three containers to mount this volume at /shared-data.

